	affiliations = {Ltd., Qingdao, Shandong, China},
	abstract = {To address the problem of ensuring passenger safety monitoring under the specific spatial constraints and occlusion conditions during urban rail transit operation, an improved human violent behavior detection method, LDST-AttnNet, is proposed. First, a backbone network is constructed using linear deformable convolution (LDConv) and Conv-LSTM modules to enhance the capability of spatial detail representation and temporal dynamic modeling. On this basis, a multi-granularity feature fusion strategy is designed to unify and integrate feature representations across different depths and temporal scales, thereby improving the model’s sensitivity to fine-grained and sudden abnormal patterns. This effectively alleviates the issues of hierarchical semantic disconnection and temporal redundancy. Furthermore, an RGB-optical flow two-stream structure combined with a dual-attention mechanism is introduced to achieve key region focus and abrupt motion awareness. Finally, the loss function is improved by using an adjustable focusing factor and weight constraints to address the class imbalance problem. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method maintains a recognition accuracy of 92.5% even in complex carriage environments with occlusions and lighting variations, showing strong behavior recognition accuracy and environmental robustness. This provides a feasible intelligent solution for passenger safety monitoring in rail transit systems. © 2025 SPIE.},
