	abstract = {Accurate cyberbullying detection requires deep semantic understanding and contextual entity relationship modeling. This paper proposes BERT-BiLSTM-KG, a novel hierarchical architecture that integrates knowledge graph enhanced representation with cross-modal attention mechanisms. The key innovations include: (1) A knowledge fusion layer combining BERT embeddings with learnable entity representations through dimension-aligned projection, enabling joint text-entity feature learning; (2) A dual attention mechanism integrating CBAM (Convolutional Block Attention Module) adapted for text processing and multi-head self-attention, forming complementary channel-spatial-semantic attention pathways; (3) A hybrid pooling strategy concatenating average, maximum, and attention-based temporal features from bidirectional LSTM outputs. The architecture implements dimensional compatibility through innovative tensor reshaping (2 D → 1 D → 2 D transformations) and establishes unified representation spaces for heterogeneous feature fusion. Experimental validation on benchmark datasets demonstrates significant performance improvements over baseline models, achieving 88% accuracy and 0.87 F1-score. The model shows particular advantages in capturing implicit malicious semantics through its entity-aware attention mechanism, with 7% higher recall on subtle bullying patterns compared to conventional BERT-BiLSTM approaches. This research provides a new paradigm for joint text-entity representation learning in social media content analysis. © 2025 IEEE.},
