	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 International Conference on Data Science and Business Systems, ICDSBS 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICDSBS63635.2025.11031972},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105011071367&doi=10.1109%2FICDSBS63635.2025.11031972&partnerID=40&md5=8b790cdb56100248c252e5fbe9f78f25},
	affiliations = {SRM Institute of Science and Technology Ramapuram Campus, School of Computing, Chennai, TN, India},
	abstract = {In neural machine translation (NMT), it is crucial to effectively handle offensive or slur words; particularly in low-resource languages like Tamil, it is all the more important to translate English words and phrases and present them in a cultural and respectful manner. In the proposed approach, the use of a context-aware NMT framework detects and translates offensive English phrases and expensive English phrases and expressions into a dignified and polite manner. The conversion includes a combination of politeness-based on dictionary mapping and transformer-based paraphrasing. The accuracy of this approach is 95.4%, and the quality, BLEU score, is 78.2. The presence of a confidence scoring mechanism produces accurate and reliable translations. The proposed approach applies well in moderation requirements for social media. Furthermore, the same approach can be used for AI-based customer support and content filtering. In low-resource languages like Tamil, the management and control of offensive languages and expressions is of utmost importance to achieve acceptable and respectful translations. © 2025 IEEE.},
