	affiliations = {University of Mumbai, Mumbai, MH, India; Pillai HOC College of Engineering and Technology, Rasayani, MH, India},
	abstract = {Ensuring children's safety in day care facilities is of utmost importance, and fast detection of violent behavior is essential for intervention and prevention. With the help of OpenCV for video processing and Convolutional and Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN) for violence recognition, we provide a real-time violence detection system in this project. The system keeps an eye on live video feeds from cameras positioned throughout the daycare facility. Real-time video analysis, frame extraction, and pre-processing are all done with OpenCV. After pre-processing, the frames are run through a CNN model that has been trained to identify violent behaviors and actions. Furthermore, sequences of frames are fed into an RNN in order to capture temporal context, which allows the model to identify patterns of aggression across time. The owner of the center and the parents of the affected kid receive notifications as soon as violence is detected, enabling rapid action to be taken to handle the problem and guarantee the safety of all children in care. © 2025 IEEE.},
