	doi = {10.1109/ICITRI62858.2024.10698923},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85207043688&doi=10.1109%2FICITRI62858.2024.10698923&partnerID=40&md5=9f6dbb4bb3b5487a200aa509c7c525be},
	affiliations = {Institut Teknologi Sepuluh Nopember, Department of Informatics, Surabaya, East Java, Indonesia},
	abstract = {With more activity on social media specifically on Twitter, hate speech and dangerous remarks with abusive, racist or discriminatory words are increasingly spreading, especially at certain moments. Identification of hate speech and dangerous speech can be done by utilizing the technology extraction feature on text. Some previous research has studied approaches to effectively identify dangerous speech. This research was made through a Systematic Literature Review approach (SLR) with the Population, Intervention, Comparison, Outcome (PICO) method which aims to identify and analyse problems around dangerous speech that is quickly spread in Indonesian Twitter posts. SLR aims to identify, evaluate, and systematically summarize existing scientific evidence on a particular research topic. The purpose of this SLR is to make it easier for researchers to confirm existing findings for future research. Through literature analysis, this paper explains the role of understanding the content of potentially dangerous messages, identifying various types of dangerous speech such as hate speech, the use of abusive language, and the speed at which messages are spread on the Twitter platform. In this study, we identified dangerous speech on the Twitter platform from studies derived from IEEE, Science Direct, and Google Scholar over the past five years from 2019 to 2024, and we found a total of 104 papers. Then from the review results, we found 33 papers that are relevant to our research objectives. The results of this literature review provide valuable insights into the dynamics and challenges of dealing with the spread of dangerous speech on social media. © 2024 IEEE.},
