	abstract = {In today's digital age, the internet has allowed people from different corners of the world to easily share their ideas. It is a fairly ubiquitous opinion that everybody must have the basic human right to share their opinion and express their thoughts and feelings. However, with this heightened connectivity, people tend to abuse their rights. People often send abusive or racist remarks over the internet, often anonymously. While research on hate speech detection is growing rapidly and diversely, detecting hate speech remains a difficult task. This paper proposes a deep learning model to detecting abuse and hate speech on online social networks. We first start by cleaning the data and then obtain the sentence embeddings using the BERT model. After this, we pass our sentence embeddings to our custom Convolutional Neural Network model to classify the tweets. We optimize the performance of our custom Convolutional Neural Network model by applying the GridSearch technique for hyperparameter tuning. This custom model has a superior performance to baseline Machine Learning Models. We have evaluated the performance of our model on the Hate Speech and Offensive Language dataset. © 2024 IEEE.},
