	abstract = {This chapter explores the potential of machine learning (ML) and natural language processing (NLP) to detect and prevent fake news and hate speech. It examines the current state of fake news and hate speech focusing on the challenges presented by the rapid pace of technological change and the difficulty in distinguishing real from fake news. It discusses the challenges faced when using ML and NLP, such as the need for large datasets and the potential for false positives. It then looks at existing software and algorithms that are being used to detect and prevent Fake News, Hate Speech, and examines their efficacy and limitations. This chapter also examines the use of machine learning and natural language processing (NLP) to detect and prevent fake news and hate speech. It then examines the various machine learning and NLP approaches that can be applied to detecting and preventing fake news and hate speech, such as deep learning, sentiment analysis, and supervised learning. The chapter also discusses the potential advantages and limitations of these approaches and the need for further research to improve the accuracy of detection and prevention of using ML and NLP to detect and prevent it. Finally, the paper suggests potential future directions for research in this area, it looks at the ethical implications of using machine learning and NLP for fake news and hate speech detection and prevention and provides some recommendations for the responsible use of these technologies. © 2024 CRC Press.},
