	affiliations = {VIT Bhopal University, School of Computing Science Engineering and Artificial Intelligence, Sehore, MP, India; Vellore Institute of Technology, School of Computer Science and Engineering, Vellore, TN, India},
	abstract = {This study addresses the pressing issue of hate speech on online platforms. Traditional text-based analysis is no longer adequate for identifying hate speech due to the growth of internet platform data. The project aims to create scalable automated methods for web platforms to detect hate speech in real-time. To find the best algorithms for recognizing hate speech, the study compares many machine learning models using a large dataset in Hindi from Twitter. Where the study matters is in the creation of advanced content filtering systems that offer a more secure and friendly online environment. Support Vector Machine (SVM) has the best performance, with outstanding precision (0.9468) and F1-score (0.944), showcasing the top-performing ones and talking about the difficulties and ways ahead in this field. The study recommends improving Hindi hate speech detection systems. With problems such as imbalanced data sets and the dynamic nature of online language, language research using hybrid models, constant model adjustments, and language trend monitoring are all necessary. © 2024 IEEE.},
