	affiliations = {Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Jyothi Enginnering College, Thrissur, India},
	abstract = {Hate speech detection is a pivotal task in maintaining a safe and inclusive online environment. This project employs a combination of Word2Vec and BERT-CNN architectures to effectively identify and classify offensive language and normal language from social media comments and texts. The project encompasses several key steps, including data preprocessing, feature extraction using Word2Vec embeddings, and model training using the BERT-CNN architecture. The BERT-CNN framework consists of six layers: BERT embedding layer, convolutional layer(s), pooling layer, dense layer, dropout layer, and output layer. Training involves optimizing the model parameters through backpropagation to minimize classification errors. Evaluation metrics are used to assess the model's performance. The trained model can be deployed to automatically detect and mitigate hate speech in real-time, thus leading to a safer and more inclusive online community. This project contributes to combating online hate speech and fostering a positive digital environment. © 2024 IEEE.},
